--TEST--
A `try` with neither `catch` nor `finally` is refused, as it is in PHP — the block would be guarded by nothing
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The shape a deleted clause leaves behind: the block still runs, nothing is
// caught, and nothing runs on the way out, so the keyword claims a guard the
// statement does not have.
try {
    echo "guarded\n";
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0242]: a `try` needs a `catch` or a `finally`
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
